description: Keep AI/editorial instructions out of published website content
alwaysApply: true
---

# Published content only

Ship visitor-facing copy only. Never put AI process notes, authoring checklists, or distribution instructions into pages, guides, or components that render on the site.

**Do not publish:**
- "After you publish…" / "share this post…" / "submit to forums…"
- "TODO", "placeholder", "for the AI", "when ready", "coming soon" as fake content filler unless the page is intentionally a stub the user asked for
- Internal SEO/AEO tactics written as if they were merchant-facing advice
- Draft scaffolding commentary ("keeps the collection valid", "replace this later") in live `draft: false` content

**Do publish:** merchant-facing product copy, guides, comparisons, and legal text.

Put operational notes in README, PR descriptions, chat, or `draft: true` content only.
